    {
      "beat_id": "B08",
      "act": "THE MECHANISM",
      "lane": "BODY",
      "narration_text": "Outward pressure — elevated fluid pressure inside the tumor — drives fluid from the core toward the rim. A large particle diffuses slowly through the dense matrix and gets shoved back by that outward current. It piles up at the vessel wall and barely moves inward.",
