      "narration_text": "Here is the example. Two mouse tumors. Each receives the same injected dose. The 150-nanometer arm achieves 6.2 percent injected dose per gram at the rim — high total accumulation. The 30-nanometer arm achieves only 2.1 percent total — but 80 percent of those particles are distributed evenly through the core. At day 21, the 150-nanometer arm shows 15 percent tumor volume reduction. The 30-nanometer arm: 72 percent. Same dose. More drug in the tumor, less kill. Distribution won.",
